# The project directory name contains a literal `&`, which cmd.exe (npm's
# default script-shell on Windows) parses as a command separator. That breaks
# every .bin shim (tsx, tsc, vitest, vite): cmd mangles the quoted path at the
# `&`, so e.g. tsx.CMD resolves to C:\Users\SESIP\Desktop\tsx\dist\cli.mjs
# (MODULE_NOT_FOUND). PowerShell handles the path correctly, so use it as the
# npm script shell for this repo only (project-local config, no global changes).
script-shell=C:\windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe
